      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing an External Provider**\n\nI've decided to proceed with OpenAI for the embedding functionality, as it's a well-established and accessible option. Now I must integrate it into the Python script to generate embedding vectors from a given text string. The script will be named `embed_text.py`.\n\n\n**Implementing the Python Script**\n\nI am now implementing the `embed_text.py` script. The initial focus is on importing the `openai` library and configuring the API key using an environment variable for security. Next, I'll define a function to produce embeddings given some text, then call it with sample text to test the integration. My current focus is ensuring the script runs successfully with OpenAI.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789866142642,
          "start": 1789866140571
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc55e39b001FlD6QR5OgC5lI2",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc55ddf5001kbM8v2kSjjQwkn",
      "session_id": "ses_f43aa228cffeSAVIrln9ZnAqXt",
      "time_created": 1789866140571,
      "time_updated": 1789866142643
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "BBuu5J3n9LKSr8TY",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import openai\nimport os\n\ndef embed_text(text: str) -> list[float]:\n    \"\"\"Generates an embedding vector for a given text string using OpenAI's API.\"\"\"\n    # Ensure the OpenAI API key is set as an environment variable\n    openai.api_key = os.environ.get(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\")\n    if not openai.api_key:\n        raise ValueError(\"OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable not set.\")\n\n    # Use a specific embedding model\n    model = \"text-embedding-ada-002\" \n\n    response = openai.embeddings.create(\n        input=text,\n        model=model\n    )\n    return response.data[0].embedding\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sample_text = \"Hello, world! This is a test sentence for embedding.\"\n    try:\n        embedding = embed_text(sample_text)\n        print(f\"Embedding for '{sample_text}' (first 5 dimensions): {embedding[:5]}...\")\n        print(f\"Embedding dimension: {len(embedding)}\")\n    except ValueError as e:\n        print(f\"Error: {e}\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\")\n",
            "filePath": "embed_text.py"
          },
